From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: build for iOS and tvOS

The AVFoundation audio output already sets up AVAudioSession on iOS and
tvOS, but it does not compile there: with HAVE_AVFOUNDATION the CoreAudio
utility and channel-map helpers declare and build the macOS-only HAL
functions (AudioDeviceID, AudioStreamID, AudioObject), and init() selects
an output device through setAudioOutputDeviceUniqueID:, which iOS and
tvOS do not have. The AudioUnit output fails too, because it includes the
same channel-map header.

Add CA_HAVE_HAL, true for the CoreAudio output and for AVFoundation on
macOS, and use it in place of HAVE_COREAUDIO || HAVE_AVFOUNDATION wherever
the code needs the HAL. The channel-layout helpers AVFoundation uses
(ca_get_acl, ca_find_standard_layout, ca_log_layout) stay available. On
iOS and tvOS the AVFoundation output then has no device list or device
selection and uses the shared AVAudioSession route, as the AudioUnit
output does.

The output also calls cfstr_get_cstr() from osdep/utils-mac.c, which
meson only builds with the macOS cocoa feature, so a static libmpv for
iOS or tvOS could not be linked into an app. Build utils-mac.c with the
AVFoundation output whenever cocoa is off. macOS builds with cocoa are
unchanged. Applies to mpv v0.41.0.

